// Core primitives are compiler-known opaque types. `is` declares a nominal refinement, and `with`
// pins the supplied-slot contract that ordinary Tao declarations fill.
primitive item

primitive number

primitive text

primitive boolean

primitive list

primitive time

// A duration is a unit value of the `duration` family; `.unit` builds and reads it (Decisions §2).
primitive duration

primitive action

primitive design

// One renderable primitive. Every declaration made with `view` has this type; what a view can do
// is inferred from its body, and how it appears is chosen where it is presented. `nav` refines it,
// so a mounted navigator goes wherever a view goes.
primitive view

primitive nav is view with {
   implement,
}

primitive datasource with {
   implement,
}

primitive app with {
   Name text,
   Navigator nav,
   Datasource datasource is none,
   Design design is none,
}
